    "q-104015": {
      "dom_id": "step-q104015",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Find the set of values of $x$ that satisfy $-8<4x-4<8$ or $2-x>3.$",
      "worked_solution": "We start by solving $-8<4x-4<8:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8 & <4x-4<8 \\\\ -4 & <4x<12 \\\\ -1 & <x<3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14237546/assets/fdf77a12d535974088d36ca7508443a2aab00bb147fde65a17fc06cf5f0bce23.png)\n\nThen, we solve $2-x>3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-x & >3 \\\\ -x & >1 \\\\ \\frac{-x}{-1} & <\\frac{1}{-1} \\\\ x & <-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14237546/assets/8a1af65f2cebbcaeb73c138be5d1cd67d714aacb8db1c995f29b930c06b953fe.png)\n\nTo graph the values of $x$ that satisfy either inequality, we overlay the two graphs on the same number line:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14237546/assets/be8cace3271cdfa133d1b647359400681db04f504560ad306e3e1807eb1502d9.png)\n\nTherefore, the final solution is $-1<x<3$ or $x<-1.$ We can write this using interval notation as $(-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (-1,3).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
